    {
      "title": "US judge dismisses Trump's multibillion-dollar defamation suit against WSJ",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-judge-dismisses-trump-s-multibillion-dollar-defamation-suit-against-wsj-126110100020_1.html",
      "description": "A federal judge has thrown out President Donald Trump's multibillion-dollar lawsuit against The Wall Street Journal and media mogul Rupert Murdoch over a story reporting on his ties to wealthy financier Jeffrey Epstein.\nUS District Judge Darrin Gayles in Miami dismissed the suit with prejudice on Saturday, ruling that the president did not prove the defendants made defamatory statements with actual malice.\nThe ruling said the lawsuit was \"grasping at straws\" as it attempted to \"manufacture\" flaws in the Journal's investigative reporting.\nWhen a case is thrown out \"with prejudice,\" it cannot be refiled again and the dismissal is permanent and incontrovertible.\nThe lawsuit was over a story the Journal published last year describing a sexually suggestive letter that the paper said bore Trump's name and was included in a 2003 album compiled for Epstein's 50th birthday.\nThe letter was reportedly collected by disgraced British socialite Ghislaine Maxwell as part of a birthday album for",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T02:43:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump defamation suit against Murdoch, WSJ over Epstein letter dismissed with prejudice",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/31/trump-murdoch-wsj-epstein-defamation-lawsuit-dismissed.html",
      "description": "President Donald Trump denied writing a birthday letter to sex offender Jeffrey Epstein, which was the subject of a 2025 Wall Street Journal article.",
      "source_name": "CNBC Top News",
      "published": "2026-10-31T23:56:40"
